[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127376,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic fibroblastoma is a benign soft tissue tumour characterized by stellate fibroblasts in a fibromyxoid background.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127377,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8810/0 Desmoplastic fibroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127378,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH2ZF3 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Desmoplastic fibroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127379,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> collagenous fibroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127380,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127381,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic fibroblastoma has a predilection for the upper extremities, although it may occur anywhere {7661281; 9670823; 8832562}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127382,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This tumour is a painless, solitary, slow-growing mass and predominantly subcutaneous, although it may involve skeletal muscle {9670823}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127383,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic fibroblastomas are rare. They predominantly affect adults (median age: 50&ndash;60&nbsp;years) and show a male predominance {7661281; 9593348; 9670823; 8832562}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127384,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127385,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic fibroblastomas have been reported to have translocations involving 11q12, including t(2;11)(q31;q12) and t(11;17)(q12;p11.2) {15036892; 19596257}. The <em>FOSL1</em> gene is located nearby (at 11q13.1), and the FOSL1 protein is overexpressed in these tumours {27442992; 22411068}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127386,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic fibroblastoma manifests as a circumscribed, firm mass with a white-grey cut surface. It can be as large as 200&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127387,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Desmoplastic fibroblastomas are hypocellular tumours with bland, spindled to stellate fibroblasts and a fibromyxoid to delicate collagenous background {7661281; 9670823; 8832562}. Immunohistochemistry is nonspecific; desmin, keratin, and CD34 are negative {8832562}. The differential diagnosis includes desmoid-type fibromatosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127388,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127389,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127390,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a hypocellular tumour with a fibromyxoid collagenous background; bland spindled to stellate fibroblasts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127391,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127392,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 387,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The behaviour of this tumour is benign, with no local recurrence after excision {7661281; 9670823; 8832562}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:44:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]